      },
      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Big agree. Yellow text in menus also just unifies the design language. It consistently communicates which users are friends and which users aren't, in any menu. That includes menus like \"Online Friends\" where, obviously everyone is your friend, so one might think the yellow would be redundant, but no; removing the yellow there makes the UI inconsistent, which causes confusion, regardless of how significant.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
